{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>May be put to any use.</b> It comes and teaches about the fat — that it does not impart the impurity of a carcass." "<b>But you shall not eat it.</b> The Torah said: let the prohibition of a carcass and torn flesh come and take effect upon the prohibition of fat — so that if one ate it, he is liable also for the negative prohibition of a carcass. And do not say that one prohibition does not take effect upon another prohibition (Zevaḥim 70a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:21.610333153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}